@ClassicLarry  I'm setting up some post-training scaling experiments, and a few raw intermediate checkpoints from the 67B-A2B 10T run would help a lot, if it's feasible on your end. Ideally at roughly 3x spacing: ~70B, ~220B, ~660B, and ~2T tokens. No cooldown needed.

Happy to pull them from wherever's easiest, GCS/CoreWeave, an HF export, whatever's least effort.

Thanks!

🤖 PR #10523 repairs assistant-only orphan closes and bumps the affected transform versions. Local DataKit download tests pass (194), as do chat normalization tests (33); the rebuilt datasets have not been materialized.

After merge, run `uv run python -m experiments.datakit.scripts.trigger_sources --sources swe-zero-12m,davinci-dev/env-native` in the data region and materialize `all_sft_sources()["swe-zero-12m"].chat_normalized`. Check repair counters and sampled assistant spans in both normalized text outputs and the SWE-ZERO chat output, then publish a versioned store if the next cooldown will use them. The current Hero mix pins `s3://marin-us-east-02a/marin/datakit/store_4d2e363d`, so transform version bumps do not change that run.

@mcwitt @Helw150: Should the next Hero cooldown use a rebuilt store with these sources? Please confirm the target store and region before the mixture rebuild.
